lld: no thread_local allocator and no std::random_device on the C kit

Failure: the lld link fails: `undefined symbol: __cxa_thread_atexit` and
`lib/liblldELF.a(InputFiles.cpp.o) has an STT_TLS symbol but doesn't have an
SHF_TLS section` (lld/include/lld/Common/Memory.h:68 declares a
thread_local SpecificAlloc; the kit has no TLS, CPA-062, and absd-c.ld no
.tdata/.tbss, which scripts/check-c-elf.py refuses anyway); and
lld/ELF/Writer.cpp:1297 constructs a std::random_device (none in the kit's
libc++) for an unseeded --shuffle-sections.
Change: with LLVM_ENABLE_THREADS off the allocator singleton is a plain
static (every platform: parallelFor* then runs on the calling thread
only); under LLVM_ABSD_KIT the unseeded shuffle takes
sys::Process::GetRandomNumber() (the kit's getentropy) as its seed.
Behaviour preserved: with threads on nothing changes; with threads off
there is one thread, so one instance is the per-thread instance; the
shuffle's seed source changes, not its distribution.
Upstreamability: the Memory.h hunk is upstreamable (threads-off builds
should not need TLS); the seed hunk needs an ABSD OS or a "no
random_device" switch.

--- a/lld/include/lld/Common/Memory.h
+++ b/lld/include/lld/Common/Memory.h
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #ifndef LLD_COMMON_MEMORY_H
 #define LLD_COMMON_MEMORY_H
 
+#include "llvm/Config/llvm-config.h"
 #include "llvm/Support/Allocator.h"
 
 namespace lld {
@@ -65,7 +66,14 @@
 template <typename T>
 inline llvm::SpecificBumpPtrAllocator<T> &
 getSpecificAllocSingletonThreadLocal() {
+#if LLVM_ENABLE_THREADS
   thread_local SpecificAlloc<T> instance;
+#else
+  // Without threads parallelFor* runs on the calling thread only, so one
+  // instance is the per-thread instance (and needs no TLS, which the ABSD
+  // C kit does not have).
+  static SpecificAlloc<T> instance;
+#endif
   return instance.alloc;
 }
 
--- a/lld/ELF/Writer.cpp
+++ b/lld/ELF/Writer.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 #include "llvm/Support/BLAKE3.h"
 #include "llvm/Support/Parallel.h"
 #include "llvm/Support/RandomNumberGenerator.h"
+#include "llvm/Support/Process.h"
 #include "llvm/Support/TimeProfiler.h"
 #include "llvm/Support/xxhash.h"
 #include <climits>
@@ -1294,7 +1295,13 @@
       // reliably.
       std::reverse(matched.begin(), matched.end());
     } else {
+#if defined(LLVM_ABSD_KIT)
+      // The C kit's libc++ has no std::random_device: an unseeded shuffle
+      // takes the process's own random number (getentropy, RDRAND).
+      std::mt19937 g(seed ? seed : llvm::sys::Process::GetRandomNumber());
+#else
       std::mt19937 g(seed ? seed : std::random_device()());
+#endif
       llvm::shuffle(matched.begin(), matched.end(), g);
     }
     size_t i = 0;
